+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) applies an array of `add`, `remove`,
+`replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test` operations and returns the result as a new value; the document and
+the patch are never mutated, and the patch is atomic (on failure nothing is returned). It throws an
+`Error` if the patch is invalid (not an array, unknown `op`, missing `path`/`value`/`from`, bad
+pointer) or an operation fails (unresolvable path, failed `test`, moving a value into its own child,
+removing the whole document). `-` is accepted only as the target of `add`.
