+
+# Decision — applyPatch is atomic, non-mutating, strict
+
+## Context
+Services apply patches to stored records; a half-applied patch or a mutated input would corrupt data.
+
+## Decision
+- Operations run on a `structuredClone` of the document; values from the patch are cloned too, so the
+  input, the patch and the result share no objects. Any failure throws and returns nothing (atomic).
+- `-` is valid only as the last token of an `add` target; `remove`, `replace`, `test`, `from` never accept it.
+- Array indices follow the same canonical rule as `resolvePointer`; `add` allows index == length.
+- `remove` of the root throws (no document would remain); `add`/`replace` at `""` replace the document.
+- `move` into its own child throws; `move` to the same path is a no-op.
+- `test` compares by deep JSON equality, ignoring object member order.
+- Members are written with `defineProperty`, so `/__proto__` is an ordinary key, never the prototype.
+- Missing `path`/`value`/`from`, unknown `op` or non-array patch throw a plain `Error`.
+
+## Consequences
+Callers can retry or discard safely on error. Cloning costs time proportional to document size.
